  (AT, "By default, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling only replaces instances that are unhealthy or unreachable based on Amazon EC2 health checks. If you turn on Elastic Load Balancing health checks, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling can replace a running instance if any of the Elastic Load Balancing load balancers you attach to the Auto Scaling group report it as unhealthy."),
